`embInf` is the bare stage embedding packaged as a Scott map. `embInf_succ` is the recursion equation: embedding into the limit from stage \(n+1\) after the stage inclusion equals embedding from stage \(n\). The underlying sequences agree at each coordinate, by climbing when both stages are earlier, by the retraction-after-inclusion identity when the coordinate sits between them, and by descending when both stages are later. `embInf_le_succ` says that for a thread the embedding of one coordinate lies below the embedding of the next, by rewriting the earlier embedding through the recursion and using monotonicity. `embInf_family_directed` says those embeddings form a directed set, because a monotone sequence indexed by the natural numbers is directed.
